            <ArticleTitle>[A rare cause of exertional dry cough: agenesis of the left pulmonary artery associated with pulmonary hypoplasia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>146</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.11604/pamj.2017.27.146.11399</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Agenesis of the left pulmonary artery associated with hypoplasia of the ipsilateral lung is a rare congenital malformation in children; it can be discovered fortuitously or because of the presence of recurrent respiratory infections. Diagnosis is based on thoracic angioscanner. Treatment is essentially conservative. We report the case of a 6-year old child with agenesis of the left pulmonary artery associated with hypoplasia of the ipsilateral lung detected because of exertional dry cough.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
